The present flow:

Student image is sent to OCR.
OCR extracts handwritten text.
The evaluator compares only the extracted text with the teacher’s key_answer.
The original image is displayed to the teacher but is not sent to the grading logic.
So:

Diagram labels may be extracted as text.
Shapes, arrows, connections, layout, circuits, graphs, maps, and visual correctness are not evaluated.
A student could draw a correct diagram but receive low marks if the written explanation is missing.
A teacher can manually inspect the uploaded image from the evaluation page.
To properly evaluate diagrams, the system would need a separate vision-based evaluation step that sends the student’s original image and the teacher’s reference diagram to a multimodal AI model